xiaomi-mipps-auth (0.21+marble2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Start the stock main fuel-gauge verifier when the battery manager is
    ready at boot or a USB-C partner is attached.
  * Leave adapter authentication to the kernel and retire the adapter
    service, udev rule and userspace client from the installed package.

 -- GhfunNiHe <131235947+GhfunNiHe@users.noreply.github.com>  Thu, 26 Nov 2026 21:52:57 +0800

xiaomi-mipps-auth (0.21+marble1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Use the marble firmware protocol for adapter authentication.
  * Run the phone's stock fuel-gauge verifier against the main gauge in
    an isolated runtime before adapter authentication.

